  "core_hypothesis": "Hodgson's archive preserves a recurrent, task-differentiated local research organization rather than a radial relationship between one European scholar and undifferentiated informants. Questions could be standardized, fieldwork delegated geographically, merchant mobility converted into research access, assistants could coordinate specialists and produce translations/titles/maps, artists could select and route specimens as well as draw them, staff could verify figures, and the private archive itself maintained circulation control. These locally produced documentary states then entered a second organized processing regime in British institutions."
